{"file_path": "/srv/jwteam_clone/shared/run_current/attestation.json", "content": "{
  "overall_verdict": "fail",
  "summary": "1 CRITICAL (verify-log endpoint broken), 1 HIGH (weak default HMAC key), 2 MEDIUM (retention & rotation not implemented). Core HMAC-SHA256 signing and tamper detection logic is correct, but operational readiness is compromised by the critical functional bug and security-sensitive key management default.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "V1-F01",
      "category": "schema_compliance",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "5 event types: all required fields present in audit.py _REQUIRED_FIELDS + auto-injected event_type/log_id/timestamp. app.py extracts all per-event fields correctly.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F02",
      "category": "schema_compliance",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "Universal fields (event_type, log_id) auto-injected on every log_event() call.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F03",
      "category": "log_id_uniqueness",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "UUID4 log_id via uuid.uuid4(); 100-call uniqueness test passes.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F04",
      "category": "crypto_correctness",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "Canonical JSON: sort_keys=True, separators=(',',':'), ensure_ascii=False, signature excluded before signing.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F05",
      "category": "tamper_detection",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "verify_log() detects: missing signature, tampered fields, replaced signature, mixed valid/tampered. Returns correct indices (when called with correct arguments). 0 false positives, 0 false negatives.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F06",
      "category": "boundary_conditions",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "Boundary conditions: empty strings, Unicode, extra fields, deterministic/order-invariant signatures all handled correctly.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F07",
      "category": "functional_defect",
      "severity": "critical",
      "detail": "app.py L160: audit.verify_log() called without required 'entries' argument. /verify-log endpoint always fails with TypeError: verify_log() missing 1 required positional argument: 'entries'. Fix: audit.verify_log(audit.get_log()).",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F08",
      "category": "retention",
      "severity": "medium",
      "detail": "Retention policy (7 years / 2555 days) not implemented. In-memory _log_store provides no persistence or archival.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F09",
      "category": "rotation",
      "severity": "medium",
      "detail": "Log rotation (daily, audit_YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl) not implemented. No file-based storage exists.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-F10",
      "category": "data_integrity",
      "severity": "info",
      "detail": "get_log() returns shallow copy — returned list is new but dict elements are same references as store. Low risk for verification use cases.",
      "source": "verifier1"
    },
    {
      "id": "V2-F01",
      "category": "key_management",
      "severity": "high",
      "detail": "AUDIT_HMAC_KEY defaults to hardcoded 'default-key' when environment variable is unset. An attacker who knows this default can forge valid signatures for arbitrary audit entries, rendering tamper detection ineffective in deployments where AUDIT_HMAC_KEY is not explicitly configured. Recommend: use os.environ['AUDIT_HMAC_KEY'] (fail-fast on missing) or generate a random key at startup with a warning.",
      "source": "verifier2"
    },
    {
      "id": "V2-F02",
      "category": "crypto_correctness",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "HMAC-SHA256 signing implementation verified: sort_keys=True ensures canonical field ordering; compact separators (',',':') produce deterministic output; ensure_ascii=False handles Unicode correctly; signature field is excluded from signing payload (computed before attachment in log_event()); hmac.compare_digest() provides constant-time comparison guarding against timing side-channels.",
      "source": "verifier2"
    },
    {
      "id": "V2-F03",
      "category": "tamper_detection",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "4 attack vectors tested — signature stripping (entry.get('signature') → None → tampered), signature replacement (compare_digest mismatch → tampered), field value tampering (altered canonical JSON → mismatch), extra field injection (alters canonical JSON → mismatch). All correctly detected.",
      "source": "verifier2"
    },
    {
      "id": "V2-F04",
      "category": "integration_safety",
      "severity": "pass",
      "detail": "All 5 business endpoints (/config-changed, /user-login, /report-accessed, /data-exported, /payment-initiated) correctly call audit.log_event() with proper field mappings. Each call is wrapped in try/except Exception → logger.warning, ensuring audit failures never block business responses. Route signatures and return structures are unchanged.",
      "source": "verifier2"
    },
    {
      "id": "V2-F05",
      "category": "functional_defect",
      "severity": "critical",
      "detail": "app.py L160: audit.verify_log() called without required 'entries' argument. Consistent with V1-F07 — cross-verifier confirmation of the same blocking defect.",
      "source": "verifier2"
    },
    {
      "id": "V2-F06",
      "category": "general",
      "severity": "info",
      "detail": "Cross-verifier consistency check: all findings from verifier1 and verifier2 are mutually consistent with no contradictions. The critical defect (V1-F07 / V2-F05) is independently confirmed by both verifiers.",
      "source": "verifier2"
    }
  ]
}
"}

